  "qHtml": "<p>State the Occupational hazards of Agriculture Workers.</p>",
  "aHtml": "<p><strong>Hazards of agricultural workers (by group):</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Infectious/zoonotic:</strong> anthrax, brucellosis, leptospirosis (paddy fields), tetanus, Q fever, rabies, hookworm infestation, other soil-transmitted helminths, skin and fungal infections, vector-borne diseases (malaria, kala-azar, filariasis in endemic areas).</li>\n<li><strong>Chemical:</strong> <strong>pesticide poisoning</strong> (organophosphate, carbamate, organochlorine, herbicides), chemical fertilisers; arsenic in irrigation water (skin lesions).</li>\n<li><strong>Respiratory (organic dusts):</strong> farmer's lung (hypersensitivity pneumonitis), bagassosis, grain/silo dust, mouldy-hay and straw exposure; aflatoxin.</li>\n<li><strong>Physical:</strong> heat stroke and dehydration, sunburn and skin cancer, exposure to cold and rain, noise and vibration (tractors, pumps).</li>\n<li><strong>Mechanical:</strong> injuries from sickles, ploughs, tractors, threshers; falls from trees; drowning; electrocution (irrigation pumps); lightning.</li>\n<li><strong>Animal-related:</strong> snakebite, bites and stings of insects/scorpions, injuries from livestock.</li>\n<li><strong>Ergonomic:</strong> back and joint pain from stooping, lifting and heavy manual work.</li>\n<li><strong>Psychosocial:</strong> stress from debt, crop failure, climate and floods; lack of access to health care.<br />\n<em>Prevention:</em> safe pesticide use and protective clothing, footwear (boots/gloves), vaccination (tetanus), deworming, health education, clean water and sanitation, safe tractor use, early treatment of snakebite, and regular health check-ups.</li>\n</ol>",
  "qText": "State the Occupational hazards of Agriculture Workers.",
  "aText": "Hazards of agricultural workers (by group): Infectious/zoonotic: anthrax, brucellosis, leptospirosis (paddy fields), tetanus, Q fever, rabies, hookworm infestation, other soil-transmitted helminths, skin and fungal infections, vector-borne diseases (malaria, kala-azar, filariasis in endemic areas). Chemical: pesticide poisoning (organophosphate, carbamate, organochlorine, herbicides), chemical fertilisers; arsenic in irrigation water (skin lesions). Respiratory (organic dusts): farmer's lung (hypersensitivity pneumonitis), bagassosis, grain/silo dust, mouldy-hay and straw exposure; aflatoxin. Physical: heat stroke and dehydration, sunburn and skin cancer, exposure to cold and rain, noise and vibration (tractors, pumps). Mechanical: injuries from sickles, ploughs, tractors, threshers; falls from trees; drowning; electrocution (irrigation pumps); lightning. Animal-related: snakebite, bites and stings of insects/scorpions, injuries from livestock. Ergonomic: back and joint pain from stooping, lifting and heavy manual work. Psychosocial: stress from debt, crop failure, climate and floods; lack of access to health care. Prevention: safe pesticide use and protective clothing, footwear (boots/gloves), vaccination (tetanus), deworming, health education, clean water and sanitation, safe tractor use, early treatment of snakebite, and regular health check-ups."
